    "sharedFrame": "Both complete images show one rectangular lattice with all12 columns and18 rows. The vertical axis divides four cells on the left and eight on the right; the horizontal axis leaves fifteen rows above and three below. The full border, negative-side lattice and bottom rows are present, not clipped or replaced by a blank panel.",
    "scale": "Horizontal4 and8 sit respectively two and four cells right of the vertical axis. Vertical4,8,12,16,20,24 occupy every second row above the horizontal axis. Labels remain associated with the correct axis and level.",
    "points": "Exactly five distinctly filled plotted markers are visible, at(1,6),(2,10),(3,14),(4,18),(5,22). Successive markers move half a cell right and two rows up. No additional upper filled marker is displayed at the guide/grid crossing or top border.",
    "guide": "The ascending oblique guide is visibly broken/dashed in both images, passes through all five markers and extends above the fifth and below the first into the frame-boundary regions. It has no oblique arrowhead or terminal-point glyph. It is not substituted by a solid line or truncated to the five-point span.",
    "axes": "Right-facing horizontal and upward vertical arrowheads are visible and distinct from plotted points. The n and subscripted a_n labels are legible near their corresponding arrows; O is clearly visible near the origin.",
    "normalWidth": "At640px all11 labels remain complete and readily readable: six vertical numbers, two horizontal numbers, n, a_n and O. No label is cut off, obscured by a marker, displaced into the wrong grid level or incoherently overlapped. All five markers remain visible against the lighter lattice.",
    "mediaIntegrity": "Both images are nonblank and show the same complete geometry and labels. No black raster failure, missing panel, unintended extra filled point or cropped frame is present.",
